WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.600
When you ask «fix this for me», the model fills the gaps with statistical guesses.

2
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:23.600
An effective instruction names four pieces: a concrete task, real context that you provide, an output format (for example, three short bullet points) and clear limits («do not add companies or dates that are not in my notes»).

3
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:29.600
Goal: build a complete instruction with no gaps that invite invention.

4
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:44.500
Compare two requests: «Make me a good CV for London» versus an instruction with your real data and explicit limits. Your task: choose the instruction that reduces invented content and gives a useful format.

5
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:52.500
Hint: the less real context you give, the more the model fills in on its own.

6
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:59.700
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
